%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 118899cb856d7e04bac83f4463fd3b31, type: 3}
  m_Name: Scene13Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AdaptiveOhmsLaw.DialogueSequence
  lines:
  - id: intro_three_pieces
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Now we know all three pieces.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 84ebe87bb565c0f46a3d10ec4e7b05ef, type: 3}
    duration: 3.5
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: piece_voltage
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: The electrical push. V, potential difference.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6cb792b27b81655449493bfdd4e50699, type: 3}
    duration: 4.7938776
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: piece_current
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: The flow. I, current.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7008e0ee968e41e408b754ec3a609adf, type: 3}
    duration: 3.5
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: piece_resistance
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: The opposition. R, resistance.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e0f44dfba2fa2d64385af38fd4eced07, type: 3}
    duration: 4.123991
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: assemble_prompt
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Start with R equals V divided by I. Drag or tap the symbols into the slots
      to express voltage V.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2d798459f2e8d0a42847c58b3a8572e6, type: 3}
    duration: 6.648299
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: law_naming
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: And the relationship connecting them is...
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 80ad6ec0927c8c742b994d1bb47f5709, type: 3}
    duration: 3.5
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: law_revealed
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Ohms Law! V equals I times R.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: aac4a13ad463a7b46b7a5f39061c5d27, type: 3}
    duration: 4.5
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: challenge_prompt
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Our wire has a resistance of five ohms. Set the voltage so the current
      becomes 0.60 amperes.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7341f9bd871c8144d80a89840f177ca4, type: 3}
    duration: 7.9980497
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: challenge_success
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Spot on! At 3.0 volts across our five-ohm wire, the current is exactly
      0.60 amperes.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e45cb2ec61c43f946b7bb9dc1779e1d0, type: 3}
    duration: 9.00313
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: condition_temp
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: For this conductor, while its temperature stays constant, voltage is directly
      proportional to current.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5b721ca70dd406d4b842ceaa7b98f46f, type: 3}
    duration: 7.18322
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: condition_constant
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: The constant connecting them is resistance.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2602ef64a4c20f040b1f180a8f4181d9, type: 3}
    duration: 4
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
  - id: finish_summary
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: We have got our law. Now let us return to the mystery that started all
      of this.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 605243d8296f3b144bc995de5ad587fe, type: 3}
    duration: 5.883673
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
